# Testing rules

- Business rules that decide something about a person (placement band, gates, bridges, learner plan generation, certification eligibility) are pure functions in `src/lib/` with Vitest tests covering every boundary (e.g. safety 8 vs 9, total 44 vs 45, 69 vs 70, 84 vs 85).
- Tests read thresholds from a settings object passed in, never from hard-coded numbers, so they keep working when management changes a threshold.
- Access rules get tests: a learner cannot read another learner's submission; a manager with department scope cannot see another department; only admin can change a role. Use a test helper that signs in as seeded test users against the dev database.
- Playwright smoke tests for: sign-in page loads, signed-out redirect, sidebar navigation, setup-pending redirect.
- Test data is synthetic. Never use real staff or client names in fixtures; use names like "Test Learner Content".
- A failing test is reported to Bharg in plain English with the likely cause. Never delete or skip a test to make the suite pass.
